Task 1: Create Cluster Sets and Apply Labels
Subtask 1.1: Understanding Cluster Sets
Cluster sets are logical groupings of clusters that allow you to organize and manage multiple clusters as a single unit. They provide:

Isolation: Separate cluster groups for different teams or environments
Policy Targeting: Apply policies to specific cluster groups
Resource Management: Manage resources across related clusters
Access Control: Control who can access which cluster groups
