Subtask 1.4: Apply Labels to Clusters
Labels help categorize and select clusters for various operations.

Apply Environment Labels
# Label the development cluster
oc label managedcluster dev-cluster environment=development

# Label the staging cluster
oc label managedcluster staging-cluster environment=staging

# Label the production cluster
oc label managedcluster prod-cluster environment=production
Apply Additional Organizational Labels
# Add region labels
oc label managedcluster dev-cluster region=us-east
oc label managedcluster staging-cluster region=us-west
oc label managedcluster prod-cluster region=us-central

# Add team ownership labels
oc label managedcluster dev-cluster team=backend-dev
oc label managedcluster staging-cluster team=qa-testing
oc label managedcluster prod-cluster team=platform-ops

# Add criticality labels
oc label managedcluster dev-cluster criticality=low
oc label managedcluster staging-cluster criticality=medium
oc label managedcluster prod-cluster criticality=high
Apply Cluster Set Labels
# Assign clusters to their respective cluster sets
oc label managedcluster dev-cluster cluster.open-cluster-management.io/clusterset=development
oc label managedcluster staging-cluster cluster.open-cluster-management.io/clusterset=staging
oc label managedcluster prod-cluster cluster.open-cluster-management.io/clusterset=production
